{
  "header": {
    "id": "assetGroup",
    "name": "AssetGroup",
    "description": "Asset Groups are \"Assemblies\" of individual Assets. This may represent a tool, mold, workcell or other collection of assets. Some Asset Groups may represent 1 instance of an assembly (if using the Serial Number). The assets within a group, maybe swapped in / out - by your tooling/maintenance department - whichever assets are part of the group, during production - will get usage applied to them.\n\nIf you are ONLY tracking Asset Group/Assemblies - the recomendation is to create an AssetGroup:Asset - since production usage will only be tracked against Assets; alternatively, you can interchange the concept of the AssetGroup for just Assets (skip creating groups).",
    "dataModelKindId": "reference"
  },
